    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented for owner identity version 2.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Identity derivation (mix in a fixed `V2` tag so every identifier changes and no v1 value recurs)**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and `identityRegion(plainRegion)` (returns e.g. `\"NSWV2\"`). Rederived `identityKey(...)` to hash `\"V2|\" + tel + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + soundex(lastName)` (still 64-hex).\n- `HouseholdId.compute(...)` \u2014 seed now `\"V2|\" + normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (still 12-hex, still shared by same lastName+postcode).\n- `AssignMemberId` \u2014 the `REGION` component now uses `Owner.identityRegion(...)`, so the memberId embeds the versioned region (`NSWV2\u2026`) while the plain region stays for user-facing fields.\n\n**User-facing fields stay plain** \u2014 `locality` (`NSW`), `timezone`, and the owner segment's derived region are untouched (they read `getLocality()`), so the `V2` tag never leaks into them.\n\n**Response shape (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`)**\n- Moved `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey` off the top level into a new nested `identity` object (`OwnerIdentity` schema \u2192 `OwnerIdentityDto`).\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n- Mapper sets `apiVersion` (constant 2) and the three nested `identity.*` fields, with inverse mappings for round-tripping.\n\n**Audit event (`AuditOwnerCreated`)** \u2014 bumped to schema version 2: added `schemaVersion: 2`, kept the id and the (now v2) memberId, and included the owner segment recomputed from the v2 identity.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The duplicate-detection pipeline (`EnsureUniqueIdentity`, `DetectPossibleDuplicate`) automatically uses the new v2 `identityKey` since both sides go through `Owner.identityKey(...)`.",
