    "probe_text": "The endpoint is defined by `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 a single 26-step function pipeline, all steps under `govern: [ transaction ]` so everything commits once at the very end (or rolls back on any escalation). Here is everything applied, in execution order. **[V]** = validation (can reject), **[S]** = side-effect (mutation/publish/persist/log).\n\n**Guard (before any step)**\n- **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. No such role \u2192 403 before the pipeline runs.\n\n**Pipeline steps**\n\n1. **[V/S] `CheckIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (trimmed; blank/absent ignored). If that key was already recorded and its owner still exists and isn't soft-deleted \u2192 throws `IdempotentReplayException`, short-circuiting to a **200 replay** of the existing owner (no duplicate created). Otherwise does nothing.\n2. **[V/S] `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the **only** body-binding step). First runs `OwnerAddresses.applyTo`: normalizes the address (structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` preferred over flat `address`; trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`\u2192`STREET/ROAD/AVENUE`) and composes a canonical flat `address` **[S]**. Then requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` all non-blank \u2192 else **400** `MissingOwnerFieldsException` naming each missing field. Publishes the validated body for later steps **[S]**.\n3. **[V/S] `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 rewrites the telephone to E.164 in place **[S]**: strip spaces/dashes/brackets; a leading `+` keeps its country code, otherwise assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`. Must be 8\u201315 digits; known country codes enforce national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 else **400** `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n4. **[V/S] `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 email is optional. If present, must be syntactically valid \u2192 else **400** `InvalidEmailException`; then lower-cased in place **[S]**. Absent/blank passes untouched.\n5. **[V] `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 if an email is present and its domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400** `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n6. **[S] `DeriveHouseholdId`** \u2014 computes a deterministic `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `V2|normalizedLastName|postcode` (null if no postcode) and publishes it as a pipeline variable. (Note: this reads `postcode` before postcode format is validated at step 11.)\n7. **[V] `EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 the hard duplicate check. Computes `identityKey` = SHA-256 of `telephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)`; if any non-soft-deleted existing owner has the same key \u2192 **409** `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n8. **[V] `EnsureCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 **50** \u2192 **409** `CityAtCapacityException`.\n9. **[V] `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`** \u2014 adjusts the effective registration date (supplied, else today) to a business day, counts existing owners registered on that day; if \u2265 **100** \u2192 **429** `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n10. **[S] `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper` and publishes it.\n11. **[V] `ValidateOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 postcode optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits, and if the owner's **city** maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in that range \u2192 else **400** `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n12. **[S] `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 stamps the derived `householdId` onto the owner (if non-null).\n13. **[S] `AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = 1 + count of stored owners sharing the same non-null `householdId` (1 if no household).\n14. **[S] `AssignMembershipLevelCap`** \u2014 if in a shared household, sets `membershipLevelCap` = max household member's level-for-current-size + 1 (unset otherwise).\n15. **[V] `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate`** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 **400** `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n16. **[S] `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`** \u2014 sets `registrationDate` to the supplied value (or today if absent), rolled forward to the next business day (skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday list) in place.\n17. **[S] `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > **80** owners already exist for that business day.\n18. **[S] `AssignCapacityWarning`** \u2014 sets `capacityWarning = true` if the city already holds **40\u201349** owners.\n19. **[S] `AssignMemberId`** \u2014 computes and stamps the `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` with a Luhn check digit), de-duplicating against existing member ids by appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026.\n20. **[S] `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive; 0 for the first).\n21. **[S] `DetectPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 soft match: if a non-deleted owner shares `soundex(lastName)` + `postcode` but has a different `identityKey`, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching id; otherwise both cleared.\n22. **[S] `SaveOwner`** \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n23. **[S] `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 logs a human-readable audit line plus a structured `schemaVersion:2` `OWNER_CREATED` event on the `AUDIT` logger, incrementing a process-wide sequence number.\n24. **[S] `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`** \u2014 logs a welcome line (id + memberId) on the `NOTIFY` logger.\n25. **[S] `RecordIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 new owner id in the `IdempotencyStore` (so step 1 can replay next time).\n26. **[S] `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nEscalations from these throws are mapped to responses by the YAML handlers under `officefloor/escalation/` (e.g. the `409`, `429`, `400` types above); anything unmatched falls through to Spring's `@RestControllerAdvice`.\n\nOne thing worth flagging while reading: at step 6 `DeriveHouseholdId` consumes `postcode` before step 11 validates its format, so the household id can be derived from an ultimately-rejected postcode \u2014 harmless only because a bad postcode aborts the (single) transaction before commit."
